                    <h1 class="blog-title text-center mb-4">AIIMS Bathinda Announces Recruitment for 163 Senior Resident Posts: Your Path to a Prestigious Medical Career!</h1>
                    <p class="lead mb-4">The All India Institute of Medical Sciences (AIIMS), Bathinda, a premier healthcare institution under the Government of India, has released a significant recruitment notification for <strong>163 non-academic Senior Resident positions</strong>. This is a golden opportunity for eligible medical and non-medical candidates seeking a challenging and rewarding career in one of India's most esteemed medical facilities.</p>

                    <p>Applications for these coveted posts are being accepted online via a dedicated Google Form until <strong>January 7, 2026</strong>. Following the online submission, candidates are also required to submit a hard copy of their application by <strong>January 12, 2026</strong>. Successful candidates will be offered an attractive salary package as per the 7th CPC, with a basic pay of up to ₹67,700 under Pay Level-11, along with other admissible allowances.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">A Golden Opportunity for Medical Professionals</h2>
                    <p>AIIMS Bathinda plays a crucial role in providing advanced medical care, education, and research. This recruitment drive for Senior Residents is part of the Government of India Residency Scheme, aiming to strengthen clinical services, teaching, and research capabilities within the institute.</p>

                    <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ <strong>Total Vacancies:</strong> 163 Senior Resident (Non-Academic) Posts</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Application Mode:</strong> Online (Google Form) &amp; Hard Copy Submission</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Online Application Deadline:</strong> January 7, 2026 (05:00 PM IST)</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Hard Copy Submission Deadline:</strong> January 12, 2026 (05:00 PM IST)</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Pay Scale:</strong> Level-11, Entry Pay ₹67,700/- Per Month + NPA (for medical candidates) + Allowances</p>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Eligibility at a Glance</h2>
                    <p>To ensure a smooth application process, candidates must meet the specific eligibility criteria as of January 7, 2026.</p>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">1. Educational Qualifications for Medical Candidates (Senior Residents)</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">
                        <ul>
                            <li>A medical qualification included in the 1st or 2nd Schedule or Part II of the 3rd Schedule of the Indian Medical Council Act, 1956.</li>
                            <li>Mandatory registration with the Central or State Medical Council.</li>
                            <li>A postgraduate degree such as MD/MS/DNB/MDS in the relevant specialty from a recognized university or institute.</li>
                        </ul>
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">2. Educational Qualifications for Non-Medical Candidates</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">
                        <p>For departments like Anatomy, Physiology, Microbiology, Pathology, and Pharmacology:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li>A Master's degree (M.Sc.) in the concerned discipline/subject from a UGC-recognized university or equivalent.</li>
                            <li>A Ph.D. in the concerned discipline/subject from an Indian or foreign university recognized by the UGC.</li>
                        </ul>
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">3. Age Limit and Relaxations</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">
                        <p>The upper age limit for Senior Residents is <strong>45 years</strong> as on January 7, 2026. Age relaxations will be applicable as per Government of India rules:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li>SC/ST: 5 years</li>
                            <li>OBC: 3 years</li>
                            <li>PwBD: 10 years</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p class="small text-muted"><em>Note: No age relaxation will be provided to SC/ST/OBC candidates applying for unreserved vacancies.</em></p>
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Department-wise Vacancy Breakdown</h2>
                    <p>The 163 vacancies are distributed across numerous medical and non-medical departments, offering a wide array of opportunities. Here’s a snapshot of the vacancies in some key departments:</p>
                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table>
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Department</th>
                                    <th>Vacancies</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr><td>Anaesthesiology</td><td>25</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>General Medicine</td><td>11</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>General Surgery</td><td>11</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>Paediatrics</td><td>11</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>Radiology (Radiodiagnosis)</td><td>7</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>Neurosurgery</td><td>6</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>Obstetrics &amp; Gynaecology</td><td>6</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>Orthopaedics</td><td>4</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>Pathology</td><td>4</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>Cardiology</td><td>3</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>Emergency Medicine</td><td>3</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>Pulmonary Medicine</td><td>6</td></tr>
