                        </table>
                    </div>
                    <p class="small text-muted"><em>For a complete department-wise breakdown, please refer to the official AIIMS Bathinda Senior Resident Recruitment 2025 Notification PDF.</em></p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Attractive Salary and Benefits</h2>
                    <p>Selected candidates will be appointed as Senior Residents under the 7th Central Pay Commission (CPC) framework.</p>
                    <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ <strong>Pay Scale:</strong> Level-11 of the Pay Matrix</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Entry Pay:</strong> ₹67,700/- Per Month</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Additional Benefits:</strong> Non-Practicing Allowance (NPA) for medical candidates, Dearness Allowance (DA), House Rent Allowance (HRA), Transport Allowance (TA), Provident Fund (PF), and other usual allowances as per Central Government rules.</p>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Your Step-by-Step Application Guide</h2>
                    <p>The application process involves both an online Google Form submission and a physical submission of a hard copy.</p>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">1. Fill the Google Form (Online Application)</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">
                        <p>The first crucial step is to complete the online application via the Google Form. This form is mandatory, and your application will not be considered without its submission. The direct link is available on the official AIIMS Bathinda website.</p>
                        <p class="highlight-text"><strong>Last Date for Google Form Submission: January 7, 2026 (05:00 PM IST)</strong></p>
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">2. Pay Application Fees</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">
                        <p>After filling the Google Form, candidates must pay the prescribed application fee through the official SBI Collect payment link (details available in the notification). Ensure you note down the transaction number.</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li><strong>For General/OBC/EWS Candidates:</strong> ₹1180/- (including GST)</li>
                            <li><strong>For SC/ST Candidates:</strong> ₹590/- (including GST)</li>
                            <li><strong>For PwBD Candidates:</strong> No Fee</li>
                        </ul>
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">3. Send Hard Copy of Application</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">
                        <p>Download the application form (Annexure attached to the official notification) from the AIIMS Bathinda website. Fill it out completely and attach self-attested copies of the following documents:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Educational Qualification Certificates</li>
                            <li>Experience Certificates (if any)</li>
                            <li>Age Proof / Date of Birth Certificate</li>
                            <li>No Objection Certificate (NOC) if currently employed</li>
                            <li>Category Certificate (if applicable)</li>
                            <li>Transaction Receipt of application fee payment</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p>The envelope containing the hard copy must be super-scribed with: <strong>“APPLICATION FOR THE POST OF Senior Resident (Non-academic) for the DEPTT. OF_____________”</strong>.</p>
                        <p>Send the complete application package via Speed Post or Registered Post to:</p>
                        <div class="highlight-text">
                            <p><strong>The Recruitment Cell, Administrative Block, Mandi Dabwali Road, AIIMS, Bathinda-151001, Punjab.</strong></p>
                        </div>
                        <p class="highlight-text"><strong>Last Date for Receipt of Hard Copy: January 12, 2026 (05:00 PM IST)</strong></p>
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Selection Process</h2>
                    <p>The selection process for the Senior Resident posts at AIIMS Bathinda will primarily involve an interview. In the event of a large number of applicants, a screening test (Computer-Based Test or Offline Test) may be conducted to short-list candidates for the interview. The final decision regarding the selection criteria and process rests with the Executive Director, AIIMS Bathinda.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Don't Miss This Opportunity!</h2>
                    <p>This recruitment drive by AIIMS Bathinda offers a remarkable chance to build a fulfilling career in a prestigious institution. With 163 vacancies and an attractive compensation package, interested and eligible medical and non-medical professionals are strongly encouraged to apply well before the deadlines. Ensure all application steps, including both online and hard copy submissions, are meticulously followed to avoid any last-minute issues. Prepare thoroughly and embark on a promising journey with AIIMS Bathinda!</p>
                 </div>
             </div>
       </div>

            
